  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Escalation of economic restrictions tied to maritime security (sanctions, export controls, financial limits) drives US and Chinese policymakers to harden and better coordinate regulatory tools and enforcement regimes for sensitive technologies, increasing the institutional strength of AI- and export-related regulation in the bilateral competition arena.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_hostilities</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_competition</data>
