<edge source="us_china_competition::geopolitical_tension" target="energy_supply_reordering::sanction_intensity" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.85</data>
  <data key="d37">Escalating US–China strategic rivalry triggers new targeted export controls, secondary-sanctions threats and more aggressive enforcement against counterparties, directly raising the intensity of sanctions applied to firms and transactions.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_competition</data>
  <data key="d40">energy_supply_reordering</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_competition::geopolitical_tension" target="energy_supply_reordering::foreign_capital_commitme" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">Heightened rivalry increases perceived political and sanction risk for investors in jurisdictions tied to the adversary, causing firms and financiers to delay, withdraw or reduce committed upstream oil project capital.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_competition</data>
  <data key="d40">energy_supply_reordering</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_competition::geopolitical_tension" target="global_bond_turmoil::market_volatility" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">Spikes in US–China geopolitical competition raise event-risk and counterparty-uncertainty that prompt rapid repositioning and stop-driven trading in fixed-income markets, directly increasing short-term bond-market price volatility.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_competition</data>
  <data key="d40">global_bond_turmoil</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_competition::geopolitical_tension" target="russia_ukraine_warfare::arms_transfer_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.75</data>
  <data key="d37">Intensified US–China strategic competition prompts the United States and partners to accelerate and expand conventional weapons transfers to Ukraine as both signaling to rivals and reassurance to allies, increasing the flow of arms into the theatre.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_competition</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_warfare</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_competition::geopolitical_tension" target="us_iran_hostilities::maritime_incident_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.75</data>
  <data key="d37">As US–China competition intensifies, US naval assets and surveillance are redeployed toward the Indo‑Pacific, reducing forward deterrence in the Persian Gulf and thereby prompting Iran to increase harassment and interdiction of commercial vessels.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_competition</data>
  <data key="d40">us_iran_hostilities</data>
</edge>
