<edge source="global_bond_turmoil::market_liquidity" target="energy_supply_reordering::supply_chain_bottleneck" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.75</data>
  <data key="d37">Tighter bond-market liquidity reduces availability of short-term funding and repo/secured financing used by traders, shipping firms and ports, increasing delays and congestion that raise supply-chain bottleneck levels for crude and equipment.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_bond_turmoil</data>
  <data key="d40">energy_supply_reordering</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_turmoil::market_liquidity" target="russia_ukraine_warfare::arms_transfer_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">A sudden drop in bond‑market liquidity increases transaction, hedging and trade‑finance costs and can interrupt FX and settlement channels used by defense firms and intermediaries, causing delays or cancellations of weapons deliveries.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_bond_turmoil</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_warfare</data>
</edge>
