<edge source="energy_supply_reordering::supply_chain_bottleneck" target="global_bond_turmoil::market_liquidity" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Worsening logistics bottlenecks force hedgers and corporates to unwind or delay positions and raise margin/cash needs, producing disorderly bond selling and wider bid-ask spreads that reduce bond-market liquidity.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">energy_supply_reordering</data>
  <data key="d40">global_bond_turmoil</data>
</edge>
<edge source="energy_supply_reordering::supply_chain_bottleneck" target="russia_ukraine_warfare::alliance_cohesion" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">Acute logistics constraints for energy (ship/port/storage shortages) force allies to compete for scarce deliveries and prioritize national allocations, producing public disputes and divergent national policies that reduce coordinated action on Ukraine.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">energy_supply_reordering</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_warfare</data>
</edge>
<edge source="energy_supply_reordering::supply_chain_bottleneck" target="us_china_competition::chip_production_capacity" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Worsening logistics and port/transport constraints for energy and specialty inputs delay delivery of fab equipment, chemicals and replacement parts and force production slowdowns or downtime at semiconductor plants, directly reducing chip throughput.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">energy_supply_reordering</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_competition</data>
</edge>
